PRJ706 provides a “Settle-Forward” solution to continue the settlement process when the ABCSettlement System or Kyndryl data centers experience a critical failure and the normal “Fix-Forward” approach is not possible.

Scope
The process starts with Pay-in Reconciliation to manually verify member obligations and identify any payouts made before the outage.
The detailed reconciliation process is out of scope and will be covered separately by ABC Operations.
This design only covers the XML-to-columnar data transformation required for reconciliation.
No process is defined to update or restore ABCSettlement PQR databases with data generated during Settle-Forward.
Once ABCSettlement is restored, the expectation is to clean up the PQR data, and Settle-Forward-generated data will not be restored.
